WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.402
Shelfmark keeps every link you save in one place.

2
00:00:01.402 --> 00:00:05.129
Open the demo: no account needed.

3
00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:10.203
Paste a link: the preview fills in by itself.

4
00:00:10.203 --> 00:00:14.500
Pick a folder, add a tag and a note.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.961
Save, and the card lands in your feed.

6
00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:24.995
Saved it before? Shelfmark tells you where.

7
00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:33.001
A pile of links? Paste them all at once.

8
00:00:33.001 --> 00:00:39.279
Folders nest inside folders; a new one starts empty.

9
00:00:39.279 --> 00:00:46.468
Give a folder a color, and search for an emoji to go with it.

10
00:00:46.468 --> 00:00:47.691
Fold a branch away and open it again.

11
00:00:47.691 --> 00:00:50.362
Pin the folders you use most.

12
00:00:50.362 --> 00:00:53.730
Drag to reorder: a line shows where it lands.

13
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.615
Unpin with one tap, Undo if you change your mind.

14
00:00:56.615 --> 00:01:00.095
Folders reorder the same way.

15
00:01:00.095 --> 00:01:02.345
A tag gathers its links from every folder.

16
00:01:02.345 --> 00:01:06.312
Rename a tag, or merge two into one.

17
00:01:06.312 --> 00:01:10.001
Star the keepers; Favorites gathers them.

18
00:01:10.001 --> 00:01:15.506
Move to folder: search the picker, the current folder is marked.

19
00:01:15.506 --> 00:01:17.795
The toast has Undo, in case it was the wrong folder.

20
00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:23.778
Or drag cards, several at once, onto a sidebar folder.

21
00:01:23.778 --> 00:01:30.821
Select links and tag them all at once…

22
00:01:30.821 --> 00:01:41.000
…favorite, copy or open them all, or move them together.

23
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.114
Need it again? Press ⌘K and type: results open under the field.

24
00:01:44.114 --> 00:01:48.018
Saved views sit above the feed: All, Videos, Articles…

25
00:01:48.018 --> 00:01:53.544
…and “Save this view” keeps any filter as a chip.

26
00:01:53.544 --> 00:01:59.400
Sort it your way, and switch between cards and a list.

27
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:05.581
Recently opened: filter, search, or pause the history.

28
00:02:05.581 --> 00:02:10.001
Nothing there? Every empty page says what to do next.

29
00:02:10.001 --> 00:02:15.726
Deleted by mistake? Undo brings it right back.

30
00:02:15.726 --> 00:02:21.626
Trash keeps what you delete; restore it any time.

31
00:02:21.626 --> 00:02:27.000
You choose how long Trash keeps it.

32
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.111
Light, dark, or Custom with your own accent color…

33
00:02:30.111 --> 00:02:35.292
…and Shelfmark keeps it readable: 4.5:1 contrast, always.

34
00:02:35.292 --> 00:02:41.780
Text size, font, density and cards, with a live preview.

35
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.954
In six languages.

36
00:02:44.954 --> 00:02:49.824
Press ? for every keyboard shortcut.

37
00:02:49.824 --> 00:02:57.002
And tell us what you think, with a screenshot if it helps.

38
00:02:57.002 --> 00:02:59.307
With an account, share a folder as a public page.

39
00:02:59.307 --> 00:03:03.050
Make it public and copy its link.

40
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:09.557
Now and then Shelfmark asks how you like it: one tap.

41
00:03:09.557 --> 00:03:12.949
Your account: the photo you sign in with, your shelf in numbers…

42
00:03:12.949 --> 00:03:16.481
…and Your data: export everything as JSON or a bookmarks file.

43
00:03:16.481 --> 00:03:18.641
Anyone with the link sees a read-only page, no account needed.

44
00:03:18.641 --> 00:03:20.644
Shelfmark. Every link, back within reach.
